        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1794306
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T20:55:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes it is",
      "parentUuid": "8e7da627_df93c0f1",
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b2b6e26_f4eab11e",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T19:53:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we make some more discrete values for that ?\n\nI don\u0027t think we should let the stack user to totally control what we put in our SMP packets.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e900447_b52e12d7",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1794306
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T20:55:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We even let users to control parameters in LE connections, but obviously only rooted users or manufacturers can control them and they are responsible for what they do.\n\nAlso it\u0027s relatively complicated to make them discrete and the size restricts what they can fianlly be. However, an alternative way is to have a checker to make sure these values are valid.",
      "parentUuid": "6b2b6e26_f4eab11e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2408cb54_ec568635",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T22:08:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We even let users to control parameters in LE connections\n\nMaybe but I didn\u0027t say that this was great as well.\n\n\u003e  but obviously only rooted users or manufacturers can control them and they are responsible for what they do.\n\nI will be our responsability when we will be Mainline as this is part of our API surface.\n\n\u003e Also it\u0027s relatively complicated to make them discrete and the size restricts what they can fianlly be. However, an alternative way is to have a checker to make sure these values are valid.\n\nI don\u0027t see where the complexity is.",
      "parentUuid": "4e900447_b52e12d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0b1fcd3_4d5f4983",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1794306
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T22:28:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For example, `auth_req`, `io_cap`, `key_size` are all plain values hard to breakdown, or you want us to make feature-based boolean properties? (Or I didn\u0027t correctly realize \"discrete\"?)\nMy initial idea is that since we can configure them in the past, then just let them be configurable in the future(instead of making properties just for some products).",
      "parentUuid": "2408cb54_ec568635",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95becffe_dd705ad7",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T22:32:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e or you want us to make feature-based boolean properties\n\nYep this is what I meant as discrete values\n\n\u003e My initial idea is that since we can configure them in the past\n\nWell, not really, it was configurable for testing with the PTS not for production usage.",
      "parentUuid": "d0b1fcd3_4d5f4983",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98b5402c_df7dd18c",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T22:33:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For example, auth_req, io_cap, key_size are all plain values hard to breakdown\n\nI don\u0027t think that `auth_req` and `key_size` should be configurable.",
      "parentUuid": "95becffe_dd705ad7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40aa3582_c4a4749f",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1794306
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T22:39:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understood(though they are usually ignored in CTKD).\nHow about just make `auth_req` and `key_dist` configurable, and assert their keys are valid?",
      "parentUuid": "98b5402c_df7dd18c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ec0407a_df42e241",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_ble.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T23:13:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`auth_req` ignoring the RFU (which I should not if we don\u0027t mask it) is 5 boolean values, so 32 possible configuration.\n`key_dist` ignoring the RFU as well is 4 boolean values, so 16 possible configuration.\n\nSo with that we offer 512 possible configurations. If we would like to do things right we should test all of them.\n\nI would prefer for us to add just one boolean flag like `quirks_disable_csrk` that would provide a workaround for only the case that we discovered (or two properties if we need two).",
      "parentUuid": "40aa3582_c4a4749f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 81,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "4da8aad839d9cfb2fe0227b36eb5b3a95f7300f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
